{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms","id":174744,"title":"Why do the Maidens hold sway over Sidereal Charms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-19T18:07:02-07:00","id":174744,"title":"Why do the Maidens hold sway over Sidereal Charms?","content":"Why do the Maidens hold sway over new Sidereal Charms? Is it simply a part of the mythos and backstory of the Sidereals, or is that backstory just a cover for a mechanical reason?<br /> <br /> It has always seemed odd to me that the Sidereals are the only type of exalt who can't make custom charms on their own initiative, they need to convince the Maidens to unlock new ones if they are desperately in need of them. I have heard that this is supposed to be balanced out by the option to make custom Sidereal Martial Arts, which I guess it does to some degree, but every other exalt type has access to custom Martial Arts as well, even if the aren't &quot;Sidereal&quot; Martial Arts. Plus I find Sidereal Martial arts tend to track into much higher power levels, while most of the the occasions when I have wanted to make custom powers were for smaller story driven things more fitting for charms.<br /> <br /> So much of what we have heard about the new edition of Exalted suggests that players taking initiative in creating charms and evocations will be a big part of the game experience. What worries me is that if Sidereals can't make custom charms, and apparently aren't very good at evocations, other types of exalts will have much more opportunity for doing player driven customization. I guess the solution would be to develop lot of resources for making custom Sidereal Martial Arts, but doesn't that kind of funnel all sidereal players into being a weird martial arts master?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T18:14:19-07:00","id":174776,"title":"","content":"IMO it's a James Bond and Q situation - James bond doesn't make his own gadgets, he does what he can with what Q gives him and makes for him. (I'm not exactly sure where I first heard the James Bond analogy, but I find it fits very well; Sidereals are agents after all). So I'd tend to think that it's a the first reason (part of the mythos).<br /> Having access to custom CMA and SMA charms feeds into their Mysterious Esoteric Sifu angle.<br /> <br /> That said, the <i>characters</i> can't make custom charms, but the <i>players</i> (and storyteller) can create some and retroactively insert them into the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T18:19:28-07:00","id":174787,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;For a job like getting rid of the drug dealer next door, I'll take a hardware store over a gun any day. Guns make you stupid; better to fight your wars with duct tape. Duct tape makes you smart.&quot; - Burn Notice, Season 1, Episode 1</i><br /> <br /> Sidereal charms are about making creative use of a limited number of tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T18:20:47-07:00","id":174788,"title":"","content":"It's absolutely and entirely because I am a control freak.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T18:30:25-07:00","id":174794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174776#post174776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the <i>characters</i> can't make custom charms, but the <i>players</i> (and storyteller) can create some and retroactively insert them into the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your right about this, and its probably how I would handle it if I was running a game with Sidereal players. But I do think that there are quite a few players and GMs who treat game books like the Bible, which can make things tricky for players who want to add customization if its not explicitly stated as a possibility. What I wouldn't mind seeing is a sidebar saying that though in the cannon of the setting a individual sidereal cannot make new charms the same way other exalts do, from a players perspective they should feel free to approach their GM with custom charms to add to the list available to Sidereal as if it was always there. This would have the same end effect of giving players opportunities for customization, while leaving the mythos of the Sidereals intact","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","user":"turkeygiant","date":". 06-19-2014, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T18:32:41-07:00","id":174796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174787#post174787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;For a job like getting rid of the drug dealer next door, I'll take a hardware store over a gun any day. Guns make you stupid; better to fight your wars with duct tape. Duct tape makes you smart.&quot; - Burn Notice, Season 1, Episode 1</i><br /> <br /> Sidereal charms are about making creative use of a limited number of tools.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd rather fight wars with Autonomous Attack Drones, but from a narrative point of view this makes a lot of sense!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T18:34:10-07:00","id":174798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174788#post174788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's absolutely and entirely because I am a control freak.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I knew it! FIGHT THE MAN!!!! errrr Maiden....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T18:41:15-07:00","id":174811,"title":"","content":"&quot;Sidereal has like super duper weird charms ! Since Joe the average gamer can't write anything more complex than an Excellency we will just gonna go ahead and do Mr.Joe the favor of not allowing him to make stupid charm so he can't dilute the weirdness that is Sidereal charms&quot;<br /> <br /> Not sure if that's what the writer's intent but some fans do seem to think like that whenever the closed-charmset discussion came up. You can add the &quot;weakness will force me to find clever ways to solve problems, I'm so smart unlike those low-IQ murder hobo gamers hur hur&quot; crowd to the problem if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 06-20-2014, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T18:48:42-07:00","id":174816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174811#post174811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Sidereal has like super duper weird charms ! Since Joe the average gamer can't write anything more complex than an Excellency we will just gonna go ahead and do you the favor of not allowing you to make stupid charm so you can't dilute the weirdness that is Sidereal charms&quot;<br /> <br /> Not sure if that what is the writer's intent but some fan do seem to think like that whenever the closed-charmset discussion came up. You can add the &quot;weakness will force me to find clever way to solve problem, I'm so smart unlike those low-IQ murder hobo gamer hur hur&quot; crowd to the problem if you want.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See I have run into this problem from both sides, playing a high essence Air Aspect magistrate, I found there was very little support for trying to capture or interrogate criminals in the charm trees, playing a off character gen Chosen of Secrets, I found that I couldn't compete with the other Exalts on the most basic elements. In both these cases having options for custom charms would make things better, whether you need to cover basic gaps, or attempt to fill specific niches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T18:51:26-07:00","id":174819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174794#post174794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your right about this, and its probably how I would handle it if I was running a game with Sidereal players. But I do think that there are quite a few players and GMs who treat game books like the Bible, which can make things tricky for players who want to add customization if its not explicitly stated as a possibility. What I wouldn't mind seeing is a sidebar saying that though in the cannon of the setting a individual sidereal cannot make new charms the same way other exalts do, from a players perspective they should feel free to approach their GM with custom charms to add to the list available to Sidereal as if it was always there. This would have the same end effect of giving players opportunities for customization, while leaving the mythos of the Sidereals intact</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree it would be wise to spell out in their book how &quot;The Maidens create custom Charms&quot; is a thematic conceit, not a moratorium on new Charms for Sidereals, if a new Charm is something the table wants. For instance, a sidebar like the following (copied and tweaked from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes/page2\">the last time</a> I posited it) would be A-OK:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;It is possible a Maiden may someday summon a player's Sidereal and demonstrate a new Charm. Perhaps the Sidereal's player wishes to include that Charm and has received Storyteller approval. With the lesson complete, the Maiden might then dismiss her Sidereal, offering no explanation for her actions. In time, it may become clear to the Star-Chosen why this Charm was taught then and there, and why to him in particular. Or the character may never understand the reason, and may take it as simply an opaque piece of the Maidens' far-reaching plans.&quot;</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T19:33:10-07:00","id":174837,"title":"","content":"The whole idea of getting the Maidens to unlock new charms was a bolt-on fix for the fact that 2e sids sucked and the game had gone careening into excessively high-powered territory where their lack of further charms actually hurt. The <i>actual</i> reason for the closed charmset is that it's a major part of the feel of playing a Sidereal, and it allows writers to do things in charm design that they couldn't otherwise, like make some charms that are &quot;too good&quot; but balanced out by the lack of effects everyone else has access to. The idea that you could expand your charmset with the Maiden's permission didn't exist at all in 1e, and it doesn't really benefit the game to have it -- the Sidereal charmset is supposed to be closed, period. The Maidens <i>could</i> in principle create more charms, but they intentionally gave you all the charms you would ever need using their uncanny foresight. 1e actually advises that if the ST really wants to introduce new charms, they be forgotten charms, or that they simply retcon the charmset as larger. This is probably wise, since it gets players out of the mindset of going to the Maidens with hat in hand.<br /> <br /> The actual goal of the closed charmset is, in short, to ensure that Sidereals have to hustle to get what they want -- they have a selection of very powerful effects, but the nature of the charmset makes it really hard to build a robust suite, so you're forced to try to find a way to twist whatever problem you're dealing with into a shape that your toolset can deal with. It isn't simply that the game doesn't want you to invent a charm to solve a problem -- it's also that it denies you basic simple meat-and-potatoes effects (or makes them complicated to use), and it wants to be sure you don't put them back in. This worked well in 1e, where the charmset was highly tuned and people didn't take ess5+ games that seriously, but it was awful in 2e because the Sidereal charmset was a hack job and the game skewed very high-essence, to the echelons where Sidderels had nothing but SMA to rely on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174816#post174816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See I have run into this problem from both sides, playing a high essence Air Aspect magistrate, I found there was very little support for trying to capture or interrogate criminals in the charm trees, playing a off character gen Chosen of Secrets, I found that I couldn't compete with the other Exalts on the most basic elements. In both these cases having options for custom charms would make things better, whether you need to cover basic gaps, or attempt to fill specific niches.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is <i>specifically</i> the sort of gap that the Sidereal charmset is designed to create. It didn't work well in 2e, but it <i>can</i> work well, and it worked about as well as anything else did in 1e. I mean, you still didn't have any charms to help you capture or interrogate criminals! But it was a lot more feasible to use the tools you did have to make do, if you were clever and resourceful. Allowing players to fill this gap with custom charms would violate the most fundamental tenet the Sidereal charmset, though -- in 1e, at least, when you don't have a power and everyone else does, it's on purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 06-19-2014, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T19:38:36-07:00","id":174840,"title":"","content":"It's there because the Sidereal charm set was designed so that the Sidereal character would have to try to find ways to use their esoteric charm set to solve problems in a different manner than the other Exalts, namely Solars, who have rather straight-forward approaches to their problems. This does not mean the player can not come up with new charms, it just means that you expressly need ST permission. I'm going to guess that was so players wouldn't just say 'to hell with it' and invent new charms that have straight-forward applications whenever they're backed into a corner, therefore diluting the thematic blah blah blah of playing a Sidereal.<br /> <br /> Sidereals were designed to appeal to a niche audience. Or at least people who have enough sense to change the things they don't like. The game isn't telling you that you're not good enough to make Sidereal charms, it's saying your character isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T20:03:41-07:00","id":174870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174837#post174837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole idea of getting the Maidens to unlock new charms was a bolt-on fix for the fact that 2e sids sucked and the game had gone careening into excessively high-powered territory where their lack of further charms actually hurt. The <i>actual</i> reason for the closed charmset is that it's a major part of the feel of playing a Sidereal, and it allows writers to do things in charm design that they couldn't otherwise, like make some charms that are &quot;too good&quot; but balanced out by the lack of effects everyone else has access to. The idea that you could expand your charmset with the Maiden's permission didn't exist at all in 1e, and it doesn't really benefit the game to have it -- the Sidereal charmset is supposed to be closed, period. The Maidens <i>could</i> in principle create more charms, but they intentionally gave you all the charms you would ever need using their uncanny foresight. 1e actually advises that if the ST really wants to introduce new charms, they be forgotten charms, or that they simply retcon the charmset as larger. This is probably wise, since it gets players out of the mindset of going to the Maidens with hat in hand.<br /> <br /> The actual goal of the closed charmset is, in short, to ensure that Sidereals have to hustle to get what they want -- they have a selection of very powerful effects, but the nature of the charmset makes it really hard to build a robust suite, so you're forced to try to find a way to twist whatever problem you're dealing with into a shape that your toolset can deal with. It isn't simply that the game doesn't want you to invent a charm to solve a problem -- it's also that it denies you basic simple meat-and-potatoes effects (or makes them complicated to use), and it wants to be sure you don't put them back in. This worked well in 1e, where the charmset was highly tuned and people didn't take ess5+ games that seriously, but it was awful in 2e because the Sidereal charmset was a hack job and the game skewed very high-essence, to the echelons where Sidderels had nothing but SMA to rely on.<br /> <br /> This is <i>specifically</i> the sort of gap that the Sidereal charmset is designed to create. It didn't work well in 2e, but it <i>can</i> work well, and it worked about as well as anything else did in 1e. I mean, you still didn't have any charms to help you capture or interrogate criminals! But it was a lot more feasible to use the tools you did have to make do, if you were clever and resourceful. Allowing players to fill this gap with custom charms would violate the most fundamental tenet the Sidereal charmset, though -- in 1e, at least, when you don't have a power and everyone else does, it's on purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok I see the point you are making, Sidereal charms shouldn't always be obviously useful, but they will be powerful, and its up to you as the player to find ways to make that power useful. This makes sense though there are two points where the concept could sometimes break down. First I think most players have the expectation that mixed play needs to be part of Exalted, and when most other splats are more obvious and direct in their power and playing very direct stories, the Sidereal can become a square peg in a round hole when trying to apply their roundabout powers in a direct campaign. Secondly there is a huge amount of pressure put on the writers to set the right tone with the content of the Sidereal Charms. The nature of the charms they write will really specifically dictate the tone of story you can tell with Sidereals, if a GM decides that they want to play on a different point on the abstract/direct scale, having the tools to make new charms would really help tailor the game system to their needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T20:27:18-07:00","id":174903,"title":"","content":"You're not really going to be able to re-wire Sidereals with a realistic amount of work, regardless of the status of the charmset. It would involve a total teardown -- you have to change charms and take them away, not just add them, and it would need to cover a fairly large proportion of the charmset. Like, just as an example, you might think that making the charmset more direct would entail changing the less direct charms to be more direct, or adding additional direct charms, but no, you have to retool the charms that are <i>already</i> direct as well, because many of those charms are intentionally &quot;too good&quot; since they're all you get. Impeding the Flow is the classic example of this. What you're suggesting is simply not a feasible house-rule without completely rewriting their charmset. Which leaves us more or less where we're at, which is &quot;if you don't like the way Sidereals work, don't use them as PCs&quot;. Alas!<br /> <br /> Sidereals actually worked very well in mixed parties in 1e -- probably <i>better</i> than they did in all-Sidereal games, so long as the party more or less got along and players didn't metagame excessively about their knowledge of how Sidereals worked. But you need to be the kind of player who wants to play a Sidereal. I don't really think there's such a thing as a &quot;direct campaign&quot; or an &quot;indirect campaign&quot; -- the ability to hustle Sidereal powers into something workable (and to enjoy the difficulty this entails, because it will be difficult) is mostly a property of the player, not the kind of game being run. A game where you have lots of time to fuck off to Heaven and do elaborate prep and then swan in out of nowhere at just the right moment is probably <i>ideal</i> in terms of making the most of Sidereal powers, but the default assumption (against which Sidereals are balanced) is that your game isn't like that.<br /> <br /> I don't really think there's a way to make Sidereals suit everybody. They're meant to appeal to a specific sort of player and if you find their playstyle irritating rather than inspiring then that probably isn't you. And there's nothing <i>wrong</i> with that, but you probably shouldn't be playing a Sidereal in that case, just as you probably shouldn't be playing a Lunar if you really hate the idea of transforming into animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 06-19-2014, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T20:53:15-07:00","id":174918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174903#post174903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not really going to be able to re-wire Sidereals with a realistic amount of work, regardless of the status of the charmset. It would involve a total teardown -- you have to change charms and take them away, not just add them, and it would need to cover a fairly large proportion of the charmset. Like, just as an example, you might think that making the charmset more direct would entail changing the less direct charms to be more direct, or adding additional direct charms, but no, you have to retool the charms that are <i>already</i> direct as well, because many of those charms are intentionally &quot;too good&quot; since they're all you get. Impeding the Flow is the classic example of this. What you're suggesting is simply not a feasible house-rule without completely rewriting their charmset. Which leaves us more or less where we're at, which is &quot;if you don't like the way Sidereals work, don't use them as PCs&quot;. Alas!<br /> <br /> Sidereals actually worked very well in mixed parties in 1e -- probably <i>better</i> than they did in all-Sidereal games, so long as the party more or less got along and players didn't metagame excessively about their knowledge of how Sidereals worked. But you need to be the kind of player who wants to play a Sidereal. I don't really think there's such a thing as a &quot;direct campaign&quot; or an &quot;indirect campaign&quot; -- the ability to hustle Sidereal powers into something workable (and to enjoy the difficulty this entails, because it will be difficult) is mostly a property of the player, not the kind of game being run. A game where you have lots of time to fuck off to Heaven and do elaborate prep and then swan in out of nowhere at just the right moment is probably <i>ideal</i> in terms of making the most of Sidereal powers, but the default assumption (against which Sidereals are balanced) is that your game isn't like that.<br /> <br /> I don't really think there's a way to make Sidereals suit everybody. They're meant to appeal to a specific sort of player and if you find their playstyle irritating rather than inspiring then that probably isn't you. And there's nothing <i>wrong</i> with that, but you probably shouldn't be playing a Sidereal in that case, just as you probably shouldn't be playing a Lunar if you really hate the idea of transforming into animals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I sometimes wish I have had a chance to play 1e. It feels like the first edition of Exalted lends a lot of context to how things are now, I mean I\u2019ve read some of the books but that\u2019s not the same as playing a game with them. Part of what frustrates me about 2e Sidereals is that they are exactly the sort of Exalt I want to play, finding solutions to problems that don\u2019t always rely on raw expressions of essence and power. Maybe they would be more appealing to me if some, not all but some, of their essence 1-2 charms were more traditional, like a Dragon-Blooded or Solar charms. That way in the situations where the very Sidereal themed charms don\u2019t apply you have a safety net for that situation other than just rolling basic attribute-ability. I don\u2019t think a few more low essence, more direct charms would compromise the secret agent of fate theme that much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T21:10:00-07:00","id":174926,"title":"","content":"The Maidens of Fate are bureaucrats who are in charge of telling everyone what to do all the time. I do not find it surprising that when they created their Exalted, they hard-coded in bureaucratic requirements and limitations on what they can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T21:29:51-07:00","id":174943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174788#post174788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's absolutely and entirely because I am a control freak.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I figured it would have been Jupiter's idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T21:50:00-07:00","id":174948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174943#post174943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I figured it would have been Jupiter's idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was, she wouldn't have let you suspect it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T22:18:53-07:00","id":174962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174918#post174918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I sometimes wish I have had a chance to play 1e. It feels like the first edition of Exalted lends a lot of context to how things are now, I mean I\u2019ve read some of the books but that\u2019s not the same as playing a game with them. Part of what frustrates me about 2e Sidereals is that they are exactly the sort of Exalt I want to play, finding solutions to problems that don\u2019t always rely on raw expressions of essence and power. Maybe they would be more appealing to me if some, not all but some, of their essence 1-2 charms were more traditional, like a Dragon-Blooded or Solar charms. That way in the situations where the very Sidereal themed charms don\u2019t apply you have a safety net for that situation other than just rolling basic attribute-ability. I don\u2019t think a few more low essence, more direct charms would compromise the secret agent of fate theme that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry you weren't missing too much. Especially with regards to Sidereals because their SMA was crazy broken compared to other people's stuff. I remember when a friend of mine GMed a game and basically managed to trivially wipe the floor with a circle of Solars using a few of the E4 charms. And when I say trivially, I mean it. The whole affair was basically the circle getting picked off one at a time while they couldn't do anything about it.<br /> <br /> And when you say you want more traditional E1-2 charms keep in mind that excellencies weren't a thing back in 1st edition so sometimes Sidereals didn't even get a dice-adder for their ability. Also, there was no social influence system so a lot of charms were basically GM fiat. Granted, that might be an improvement over 2nd edition, but you run into the same problem with some of their divination charms and other things that were very unusual. To make matters worse, there really wasn't a base-line for charm effects so when you're asking for more low essence direct charms that doesn't really mean anything in 1st edition because stuff like that really didn't exist for anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T22:28:25-07:00","id":174989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174926#post174926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Maidens of Fate are bureaucrats who are in charge of telling everyone what to do all the time. I do not find it surprising that when they created their Exalted, they hard-coded in bureaucratic requirements and limitations on what they can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda think it might not be a bad idea to re-characterize the Maidens as Heaven's spec-ops/spy masters rather than master bureaucrats. I know that you could say the Maidens already fill those roles and the bureaucracy is just a guise, but many of their charms feel like they belong a pencil pusher not a master spy. Maybe the best way to put it would be that the Maidens should appear to be the directors of the Celestial Bureaucracy, but the charms they give to the Sidereals reflect more their true nature as spec-ops/spy masters. This is just me spit-balling though I haven't put a ton of thought into this...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T22:35:23-07:00","id":174993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ithle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174962#post174962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And when you say you want more traditional E1-2 charms keep in mind that excellencies weren't a thing back in 1st edition so sometimes Sidereals didn't even get a dice-adder for their ability. Also, there was no social influence system so a lot of charms were basically GM fiat. Granted, that might be an improvement over 2nd edition, but you run into the same problem with some of their divination charms and other things that were very unusual. To make matters worse, there really wasn't a base-line for charm effects so when you're asking for more low essence direct charms that doesn't really mean anything in 1st edition because stuff like that really didn't exist for anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I wasn't really clear, the more basic essence 1-2 charms was more of an idea of what could have been done in 2e, or even as a potential idea for EX3. I have a feeling that all my speculation might be moot in the end, I think the best thing we could hope for in EX3 is a complete re-vamp of the Sidereals giving equal design weight to how they interact with other splats, and how they interact with a traditional Sidereal game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T23:49:40-07:00","id":175020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174993#post174993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry I wasn't really clear, the more basic essence 1-2 charms was more of an idea of what could have been done in 2e, or even as a potential idea for EX3. I have a feeling that all my speculation might be moot in the end, I think the best thing we could hope for in EX3 is a complete re-vamp of the Sidereals giving equal design weight to how they interact with other splats, and how they interact with a traditional Sidereal game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals worked as PCs in First edition because unless the ST was either inexperience, lazy, or personally hated the idea of sidereals (Which why would he allow such a character in the first place) their abilities were checked and balanced by the ST. Because of that the effects were usually balanced a lot more fairly than when used against a PC to cause some form of drama or challenge. When you use these effects against an NPC how strong they might be isn't the same as when used against a PC. When Sidereals got a lot of flack it was because the charmset had a number of effects PC's couldn't deflect without making a custom charm. The charmset still worked well even with it's flaws. They had a few die adders and a number of TN reducing charms that pretty much offset the issues. Along with Sidereal Astrology which while it was never good in either edition had a bigger impact because there were no excellencies. SMA was powerful but no one really got to use it.<br /> <br /> In 2e, we had pretty awful writers who weren't really good with mechanical balance so we got an extremely lazy port which made them weaker than Dragon-blooded in everything but Martial arts. They were practically unplayable. 2.5 still really didn't fix them and Astrology still being terrible didn't help either.<br /> <br /> Looking at the current situation, they'll probably have a limited charmset. Possibly with the fewest set of charms but with the solar dodge tree looking like it has 20ish charms from the spoiler in update 45. I think we'll probably be able to keep a number of old effects while adding new ones. However, sidereals will probably be developed last again because there charms more than others have to be balanced around other charmsets because of it's nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 06-20-2014, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T00:33:19-07:00","id":175033,"title":"","content":"I imagine that in 3rd edition the Sidereal charmset, while still being closed, will be much much larger than in previous editions, allowing more diversity amongst PCs while still keeping the sidereal &quot;feel&quot; of secret agent fate ninja kung-fu bureaucratic sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T04:03:40-07:00","id":175124,"title":"","content":"I always understood it as a side effect of the sidereal charms being special effects directly keyed off the constellations, thus the maidens. These charms are independent of the Sidereals - the Sidereals can use them, but not really develop them, as this would sort of be changing the maidens themselves. The sidereals could only make charms based off their own enlightened understanding of Creation and the principles behind it, which are represented as martial arts charms or sorcery.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of it, although it wouldn't hurt if sidereals had more effects of their own, either via expanded sorcery or as a third category of &quot;open&quot; charms that the sidereals themselves designed to augment their skillset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T04:56:39-07:00","id":175140,"title":"","content":"It's always funny seeing the sidereal charmset compared to SMA because it's like &quot;The sids are a bit weak when it comes to high power stuff, we should give them something to let them keep up&quot;<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> &quot;We have overcompensated to a disastrous degree.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T10:04:56-07:00","id":175320,"title":"","content":"I always felt that the Sidereals closed charm set was a brilliant way to engage the feel of them. First of all, have a look at the Charms in the Presence tree:<br /> <br /> Force Decision: If a target is trying to make a decision about something, he chooses whichever option the Sidereal wants.<br /> Impose Motivation: The target gains your Motivation in addition to his own if you win a roll.<br /> <br /> Those are amazingly powerful charms, and they aren't exactly high essence: Both are Essence 2. I'd almost call them broken, but they are a little tricky to use. There's another charm where you convince someone that you are lying. That charm is also incredibly powerful, if used properly.<br /> <br /> Part of the feel of the Sidereals is the feeling I have every day working in business: I don't have the tools I need, and I can't just go and get new software without running it through just about every damn department, and by the time they are ready to move, the software is obsolete. It really feels like I am an overworked celestial bureaucratic fate ninja trying to save the world despite itself, and that's how the Sidereals are supposed to feel.<br /> <br /> Remember that episode in Babylon 5 where Sheridan is trying to convince the League to let him use the White Star fleet to protect them, but he knows if he just says that, they'll refuse? So he tricks them into basically forcing him to put them there, while he resists it at every step, and then at the end capitulates just a little bit too easily, and then is screaming YES! at the end of the episode? That is how playing a Sidereal is supposed to work (not saying that is how it actually works). Oh, and the part where he says 'There is no invisible fleet threatening your territory.'? That's where he TOTALLY used the Sidereal 'I am lying' charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T13:09:03-07:00","id":175498,"title":"","content":"I think the closed Charm set gets a bit over thought sometimes.<br /> <br /> From what I can gather of Jenna Moran's comments, I get the impression that the original design mandate of &quot;short, powerful trees, but that's all you get&quot; was primarily just for the sake of making Sidereals mechanically distinct, in a manner reasonably informed by their setting place and function and genre aesthetics. The <i>degree</i> to which they're quirky and intricately interlocking is a matter of the touch of Jenna Moran, both in terms of her usual artistic flair and computer science background. The idea that they're designed by the Maidens, who need to be petitioned to for new ones, is a mostly incidental, if fitting, little mythology quirk.<br /> <br /> I have started to think that the degree to which they're about &quot;solve problems with toothpicks and duct tape&quot; is also overstated a bit as well. Between comments from Jenna and John, I'm in a mindset that the limitations of the Sidereals have more to do with what they can't do than what they can; as she said, sometimes you had Sidereals who had to face the Ebon Dragon armed with nothing but their own Charms, and they were generally screwed. If their Charms are toothpicks and duct tape, then they're probably mostly about picking teeth and patching things up; maybe sometimes you can be all MacGyver, but I think most of the time when facing that kind of situation you're supposed to leave the duct tape and toothpicks in the box, and instead pull out the prescience and influencing people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-20-2014, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T15:07:59-07:00","id":175562,"title":"","content":"In character, I think because Sidereal Charm trees are mystical, skill driven expressions of a short, finite, interpretable poem on the nature of reality, expressed by the Maiden. Each Charm is part of the poem (and the poem explains part of the nature of the Maiden). That's just what they are. <br /> <br /> You can't really glue or grow new magic on the edges of that. You have to go and write a new poem, and that's what the Sidereals do with their martial arts (as much as that might, arguably, be a bit ropey for social and mental skills).<br /> <br /> So it's not like &quot;Sidereals are banned from making new Charms&quot; as such, just making new Charms doesn't sit with the form of how their magic works (and could the Maidens have made them another way? who knows, the Maidens are pretty inscrutable that way). <br /> <br /> Out of character, because Sidereals are quite a bit about being awesome because they use their power more efficiently and are about working deftly under the constraints of Fate, to make things work out how they want anyway (or not). It probably helps them feel this way if they have *some* restrictions on pulling out new magic, even though with martial arts and sorcery and astrology, these are obviously far from total.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T19:07:06-07:00","id":175679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174870#post174870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First I think most players have the expectation that mixed play needs to be part of Exalted, and when most other splats are more obvious and direct in their power and playing very direct stories, the Sidereal can become a square peg in a round hole when trying to apply their roundabout powers in a direct campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, other players can have a blast using their broader-but-weaker Charms to turn the problem into a situation that the Sidereal's finicky-but-powerful Charms can fix.<br /> <br /> Jolly cooperation!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T22:26:19-07:00","id":175784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174837#post174837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that you could expand your charmset with the Maiden's permission didn't exist at all in 1e, and it doesn't really benefit the game to have it -- the Sidereal charmset is supposed to be closed, period.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would disagree; what doesn't benefit the game is having a splat that is implicitly &quot;Martial Arts and/or Sorcery or GTFO&quot;. That's why we see things like Murder Moving Fingers Dance, which has absolutely no damn business as a Martial Arts Charm, being written up as a Martial Arts Charm. There needs to be some kinda out for it, even if it's just &quot;Yeah, there's a new Charm but it's really been there all along. What are you complaining about? You're Sidereals, nothing is supposed to make any goddamn sense. Your homework for next game session is to watch <i>Twin Peaks</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think another reason that Sidereal Charms didn't fair too well in 2e is that it seemed to adopt a more...frantic pace. &quot;The Reclamation is happening <i>right now</i>. At the same time, the Underworld is invading. Concurrently, Transformers have appeared in the Southwest. In a similar fourth dimensional time plane, a new Balorian Crusade is on the verge of breaking out. And the Realm collapsed 23 minutes ago. <i>What are you doing hurry move move move move move</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Who has time to cool their heels for five days while the Wood Spirits make you friendship bracelets?<br /> <br /> ...come to think, who has time to wait five days for <i>any</i> investigation? Just doing mundane investigation is far more efficient; the only real use I ever found for Embracing Life Method, love the concept, don't get me wrong, was for metagamy bullshit like &quot;Why do the Solars of my acquaintance seem to become massive dickbags seemingly at random?&quot; and &quot;What's with these jackasses with the Yozi marks on their foreheads?&quot;<br /> <br /> I believe I had a point in there somewhere. Possibly about cheese.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=174870#post174870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First I think most players have the expectation that mixed play needs to be part of Exalted, and when most other splats are more obvious and direct in their power and playing very direct stories, the Sidereal can become a square peg in a round hole when trying to apply their roundabout powers in a direct campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think the expectation that mixed play needs to be part of Exalted is a good thing, and something that should be built into the game line as much as possible. I mean, some of my friends enjoy playing Solars but I would rather have a root canal while someone was shoving bamboo shoots under my fingernails than ever touch one again*. So what do we do when we all want to play Exalted?<br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*Although due to the loss of a bet I have, under duress, agreed to at least find something offensive about 3e Solars before I start hating on them.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T23:47:47-07:00","id":175832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=175784#post175784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would disagree; what doesn't benefit the game is having a splat that is implicitly &quot;Martial Arts and/or Sorcery or GTFO&quot;. That's why we see things like Murder Moving Fingers Dance, which has absolutely no damn business as a Martial Arts Charm, being written up as a Martial Arts Charm. There needs to be some kinda out for it, even if it's just &quot;Yeah, there's a new Charm but it's really been there all along. What are you complaining about? You're Sidereals, nothing is supposed to make any goddamn sense. Your homework for next game session is to watch <i>Twin Peaks</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think another reason that Sidereal Charms didn't fair too well in 2e is that it seemed to adopt a more...frantic pace. &quot;The Reclamation is happening <i>right now</i>. At the same time, the Underworld is invading. Concurrently, Transformers have appeared in the Southwest. In a similar fourth dimensional time plane, a new Balorian Crusade is on the verge of breaking out. And the Realm collapsed 23 minutes ago. <i>What are you doing hurry move move move move move</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Who has time to cool their heels for five days while the Wood Spirits make you friendship bracelets?<br /> <br /> ...come to think, who has time to wait five days for <i>any</i> investigation? Just doing mundane investigation is far more efficient; the only real use I ever found for Embracing Life Method, love the concept, don't get me wrong, was for metagamy bullshit like &quot;Why do the Solars of my acquaintance seem to become massive dickbags seemingly at random?&quot; and &quot;What's with these jackasses with the Yozi marks on their foreheads?&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>These are all good points, there's gotta be a place of finding a balance between ease of play and making Sidereal players work a little outside the box. From what I understand 1e might have done it a little better than 2e, but I think there's probably a lot of room for EX3 to be much better than both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T00:03:59-07:00","id":175834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=175498#post175498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have started to think that the degree to which they're about &quot;solve problems with toothpicks and duct tape&quot; is also overstated a bit as well. Between comments from Jenna and John, I'm in a mindset that the limitations of the Sidereals have more to do with what they can't do than what they can; as she said, sometimes you had Sidereals who had to face the Ebon Dragon armed with nothing but their own Charms, and they were generally screwed. If their Charms are toothpicks and duct tape, then they're probably mostly about picking teeth and patching things up; maybe sometimes you can be all MacGyver, but I think most of the time when facing that kind of situation you're supposed to leave the duct tape and toothpicks in the box, and instead pull out the prescience and influencing people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it would be better if their charms were a little more James Bond, a little less MacGyver. Sure MacGyver is fun but it really strains the limits of \u201csuspending disbelief\u201d that this top agent gets sent on such dangerous missions with absolutely no support whatsoever. James Bond on the other hand has laser watches, and explosive pens, certainly strange tools, but no one would ever say he gets sent on missions unprepared.<br /> <br /> You would think that if the maidens really wanted the Sidereals to be effective representatives they wouldn\u2019t give them charms that intentionally challenge them or even put them at a disadvantage. Instead I would imagine they would give them the Q gadget equivalent of charms, very effective tools hidden in surreptitious and surprising packages. Sidereal Ride Charms shouldn\u2019t turn your familiar into a whiney little bureaucrat, it should instead give him machine gun eyes, spinning tire cutters, and the optional oil slick function!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T08:22:14-07:00","id":176013,"title":"","content":"Just to segue from the current vein of discussion for a moment - I personally think of the Sidereal charms as being written into the stars directly, much as Astrology is. That means to create a new charm (or Astrological effect) being the scope of what is already available means altering the night sky, and we know what happened the last time the Sidereals banded together to pull that off without assistance from the Maidens - they managed to break one of the constellations (on a side note, I also like the idea that the Jade Prison itself is related to breaking the Mask, hiding fate from the Solar Exaltations [so they couldn't find a new host of heroes to empower]) I<br /> <br /> t's a bit rambly, and phone (un)formatted, but my thoughts on the matter.<br /> <br /> TLDR: they could make new charms without approval from upstairs, but they might break the sky again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":649,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/649-nightwinder","user":"Nightwinder","date":". 06-21-2014, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/649-nightwinder","name":"Nightwinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T08:52:18-07:00","id":176041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=175834#post175834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it would be better if their charms were a little more James Bond, a little less MacGyver.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean they're not?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You would think that if the maidens really wanted the Sidereals to be effective representatives they wouldn\u2019t give them charms that intentionally challenge them or even put them at a disadvantage. </div> </div> </div>No one ever became <i>more </i>challenged or disadvantaged by gaining a Charm. A Charm always provides a new advantage, ability or edge that the character never had before. And the Maidens gave their Chosen a lot of powerful Charms.<br /> <br /> You might complain that the Maidens gave their Chosen a sub-par Charm-<i>set</i>, but that supposes the Maidens could have given the Sidereals anything different if they <i>really </i>wanted to. Which is like saying that Solars can't extend their necks like silly-putty because the Sun didn't care for it, or Lunars can't craft stuff real well because Luna didn't want them to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Instead I would imagine they would give them the Q gadget equivalent of charms, very effective tools hidden in surreptitious and surprising packages. </div> </div> </div>Again, that is what Sidereal Charms already are.<br /> <br /> But notice that Q doesn't give Bond an endless number of tools for every possible and even every <i>implausible </i>event that might happen on his missions. He instead gives Bond a finite number of tools, and Bond might find himself in a situation where none of them directly apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T10:01:42-07:00","id":176094,"title":"","content":"Gods aren't all built off a template. The Maidens are extremely different from Luna and the Unconquered Sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T10:26:37-07:00","id":176111,"title":"","content":"Okay, before we continue, can we please get the &quot;Sidereal Charms are sooooo weeeiiiiirrrddd&quot; thing to die in a fire? I made an entire thread about this before, but with only a few exceptions, 2e Sidereal Charms were no more odd than, say, Clover Can't Be Found (A Lunar Appearance Charm that lets you disappear in a crowd), or Know the Soul's Price (the Solar Investigation Charm that lets you <i>buy peoples' souls</i>). The <i>insistence</i> by some Sidereal fans that Sidereals are the duct-tape-and-screwdriver Exalted continues to baffle me, especially when they manage to forget about the occasional weirdness from other Charm sets (hey, let me take this Dragon-Blooded Performance Charm to be invisible!).<br /> <br /> Look, the idea of a deliberately limited Charm set with an unusual, slightly-overpowered construction is, if not good, then at least interesting in theory. In practice, the hard in-canon limit on Sidereal Charms has caused <i>way</i> more harm than good, essentially preventing high-level Sidereal games that don't involve everyone being master Martial Artists or Sorcerers, and ensuring Sidereal players didn't get any new Charms until <i>Glories of the Most Motherfucking High.</i> And even then, they had to use the Astrological Charm and Martial Arts workarounds to get that much new stuff in.<br /> <br /> We've done the experiment. We've used the limited Charm set approach. <i>It failed</i>. So can we just skip it this time around? Please? So I can play a Sidereal without having to battle my ST over getting new Charms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T10:40:48-07:00","id":176146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=176111#post176111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, before we continue, can we please get the &quot;Sidereal Charms are sooooo weeeiiiiirrrddd&quot; thing to die in a fire? I made an entire thread about this before, but with only a few exceptions, 2e Sidereal Charms were no more odd than, say, Clover Can't Be Found (A Lunar Appearance Charm that lets you disappear in a crowd), or Know the Soul's Price (the Solar Investigation Charm that lets you <i>buy peoples' souls</i>). The <i>insistence</i> by some Sidereal fans that Sidereals are the duct-tape-and-screwdriver Exalted continues to baffle me, especially when they manage to forget about the occasional weirdness from other Charm sets (hey, let me take this Dragon-Blooded Performance Charm to be invisible!).</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't care to argue about it at the time, but I disagreed with most of the premises you presented in that thread, and it gave me an impression that you were not looking that deeply into the charmset and weren't thinking about the interactions at the charmset-level or how Sidereal charm use would fit into the context of ongoing play. The fandom tends to exaggerate the meme, but it's very much a thing.<br /> <br /> I see you're focusing on 2e Sidereals here, though, and I really need to emphasize: <i>2e Sidereals were not designed.</i> 1e Sidereals were designed, but 2e Sidereals only hit the niche of 1e Sidereals here and there, where they managed to carry it forward by accident. 2.5 was obviously done with some care, but it was a band-aid level solution that was unable to make overarching design decisions. You can't really talk usefully about the merits of the Sidereal charm structure in a 2e context at all. That's just how it turned out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 06-21-2014, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T11:13:47-07:00","id":176221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=176146#post176146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see you're focusing on 2e Sidereals here, though, and I really need to emphasize: <i>2e Sidereals were not designed.</i> 1e Sidereals were designed, but 2e Sidereals only hit the niche of 1e Sidereals here and there, where they managed to carry it forward by accident. 2.5 was obviously done with some care, but it was a band-aid level solution that was unable to make overarching design decisions. You can't really talk usefully about the merits of the Sidereal charm structure in a 2e context at all. That's just how it turned out!</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't I focus on 2E Sidereals? Yeah, I get they're the New Coke of Sidereals, compared to the original formula of 1st Edition, but that's the version that I'm familiar with, and I imagine it's the same for many other people here. Any design done for 3e must be done with the failures of 2e in mind, and one of those failures was the inability to accommodate long-running or high-powered games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T11:25:18-07:00","id":176245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=176146#post176146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't care to argue about it at the time, but I disagreed with most of the premises you presented in that thread, and it gave me an impression that you were not looking that deeply into the charmset and weren't thinking about the interactions at the charmset-level or how Sidereal charm use would fit into the context of ongoing play. The fandom tends to exaggerate the meme, but it's very much a thing.<br /> <br /> I see you're focusing on 2e Sidereals here, though, and I really need to emphasize: <i>2e Sidereals were not designed.</i> 1e Sidereals were designed, but 2e Sidereals only hit the niche of 1e Sidereals here and there, where they managed to carry it forward by accident. 2.5 was obviously done with some care, but it was a band-aid level solution that was unable to make overarching design decisions. You can't really talk usefully about the merits of the Sidereal charm structure in a 2e context at all. That's just how it turned out!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my thoughts on the matter as well. Especially considering that in 3e Essence 6 isn't something that you can hit in most games and when you do it'll be a whole different ballgame now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T14:37:18-07:00","id":176432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=176221#post176221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't I focus on 2E Sidereals? Yeah, I get they're the New Coke of Sidereals, compared to the original formula of 1st Edition, but that's the version that I'm familiar with, and I imagine it's the same for many other people here. Any design done for 3e must be done with the failures of 2e in mind, and one of those failures was the inability to accommodate long-running or high-powered games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it depends on the context. If you want to talk about the merits of the ideas that motivated Sidereal design, you <i>do</i> need to look at the case where it's worked best. Saying that &quot;we've tried this and it didn't work&quot; because it didn't work in 2e is sort of like saying &quot;I've tried wearing clothing to protect my feet and it was proved a failure&quot; because you bought secondhand shoes two sizes too small for you, then wore them without laces and made some cuts along the sides to make room for your foot. It's all well and good to talk about 2e Sidereals, in other words, but it's important you not conflate the flaws of 2e SIdereals with flaws of the philosophy that motivated the Sidereal charmset originally, and that you recognize that the way people talk about Sidereals is largely inherited from First Edition -- both because Sidereals were unplayable for the majority of 2e and thus most people who played them did it in 1e, and also because those ideas do echo forward to a limited extent in their 2e charmset, purely by accident.<br /> <br /> In 1e, the idea of an Essence 5+ game was largely conjectural -- &quot;high power&quot; was Ess 4-5. 3e seems to be returning to this model. In 1e, Sidereals had <i>way</i> more Ess 4-5 charms in their hardback than Solars did in core, because the game was meant to carry you all the way to high power, and that was what &quot;high power&quot; was. Elder essence was an undiscovered country that largely existed for the aesthetic effect it had on the actual game, so it was never really meant to have serious support in a system compatible with the regular game. 2e changed this without recalibrating the Sidereal charmset to match, but I think it's probably better to just re-establish Essence 1-5 as the &quot;real&quot; game, with 4-5 being the &quot;ridiculously high-powered endgame&quot; level, and in that context, Sids are pretty well supplied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 06-21-2014, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T19:30:50-07:00","id":176645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=176432#post176432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it depends on the context. If you want to talk about the merits of the ideas that motivated Sidereal design, you <i>do</i> need to look at the case where it's worked best. Saying that &quot;we've tried this and it didn't work&quot; because it didn't work in 2e is sort of like saying &quot;I've tried wearing clothing to protect my feet and it was proved a failure&quot; because you bought secondhand shoes two sizes too small for you, then wore them without laces and made some cuts along the sides to make room for your foot. It's all well and good to talk about 2e Sidereals, in other words, but it's important you not conflate the flaws of 2e SIdereals with flaws of the philosophy that motivated the Sidereal charmset originally, and that you recognize that the way people talk about Sidereals is largely inherited from First Edition -- both because Sidereals were unplayable for the majority of 2e and thus most people who played them did it in 1e, and also because those ideas do echo forward to a limited extent in their 2e charmset, purely by accident.<br /> <br /> In 1e, the idea of an Essence 5+ game was largely conjectural -- &quot;high power&quot; was Ess 4-5. 3e seems to be returning to this model. In 1e, Sidereals had <i>way</i> more Ess 4-5 charms in their hardback than Solars did in core, because the game was meant to carry you all the way to high power, and that was what &quot;high power&quot; was. Elder essence was an undiscovered country that largely existed for the aesthetic effect it had on the actual game, so it was never really meant to have serious support in a system compatible with the regular game. 2e changed this without recalibrating the Sidereal charmset to match, but I think it's probably better to just re-establish Essence 1-5 as the &quot;real&quot; game, with 4-5 being the &quot;ridiculously high-powered endgame&quot; level, and in that context, Sids are pretty well supplied.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to say whether 1e Sidereals were successful in their purpose. They effectively existed in a vacuum, released late in the line where they didn't need to prove their effectiveness against an evolving game line. Yeah, 2e Sidereals were broken from the get-go, but I'd like to see the 1e Sidereal set put through its paces in a post-GotMH and DotFA scenario, where everyone else's Charm sets continue to expand and theirs just... stays still.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal Charm set is fixed in place to fit a specific thematic niche, and it is one that is remarkably unadaptable. For it to function, there can be <i>no</i> evolution of the game line, making everything as stagnant as itself. If the game evolves, by introducing new mechanics or that higher level of power they say they won't introduce, it all goes to hell, and either the closed Charm set has to go, or the Sidereals will forever fall behind. And if you say &quot;well, people can just ask the Maidens for new Charms, or you can introduce it retroactively,&quot; that's not actually a closed Charm set, it's just a neat but mechanically meaningless piece of fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T20:03:14-07:00","id":176653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=176041#post176041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one ever became <i>more </i>challenged or disadvantaged by gaining a Charm. A Charm always provides a new advantage, ability or edge that the character never had before. And the Maidens gave their Chosen a lot of powerful Charms.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't entirely agree with this. Sure having a charm is better than having no charm at all, but there were some charms that were so prohibitively complex or punitive to use that they were hardly worthwhile. Essentially all they did was take up a spot in the tree that could have been filled by a better charm, as you would have had a hell of a time ever finding a situation to use the original. A lot of the charms with this problem were made substantially better by errata, but in a stop-gap sort of way, not really addressing the issue, just smoothing it over a bit. Sidereal charms can be strange and require outside the box thinking to use, but they need to maintain a balance of utility with the charms available to other exalts, a charm that requires you to work much harder to find ways to apply its power is quantitatively less useful than a charm that has a very direct and common function. Even if the Sidereal charm is more powerful that doesn\u2019t mean much if you may never get to use it. Much of the Sidereal charm set follows this pattern, which for many people diminishes the set as a whole.<br /> <br /> Taking things back to James Bond again, if Q gives him a gadget at the beginning of the movie you damn well know it is going to be useful by the end of the movie, on the other hand it sometimes feels like the Maidens give out as many \u201ccones of silence\u201d as they do Aston Martins.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T20:19:01-07:00","id":176665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=176645#post176645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereal Charm set is fixed in place to fit a specific thematic niche, and it is one that is remarkably unadaptable. For it to function, there can be <i>no</i> evolution of the game line, making everything as stagnant as itself. If the game evolves, by introducing new mechanics or that higher level of power they say they won't introduce, it all goes to hell, and either the closed Charm set has to go, or the Sidereals will forever fall behind. And if you say &quot;well, people can just ask the Maidens for new Charms, or you can introduce it retroactively,&quot; that's not actually a closed Charm set, it's just a neat but mechanically meaningless piece of fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I distinctly remember one of the devs commenting that, while the Sidereal charmset will remain closed, they wont not add new charms if the game evolves to require them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T20:46:39-07:00","id":176679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=176665#post176665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I distinctly remember one of the devs commenting that, while the Sidereal charmset will remain closed, they wont not add new charms if the game evolves to require them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this, though am too tied to hunt down the quote. Later books will retroactively add charms to their set if needed.<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Charms#Sidereal_Charms\" target=\"_blank\">found it anyway</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Q: About the fixed charmset--</i><br /> <i>Is there any chance that that won't be a thing the writers choose to feel bound by?</i><br /> <i>Eg, it's a fixed charmset in the logic of the world, but not in a way that prevents publication of new charms?</i><br /> <i>I totally get the 'fix this problem with a spatula, a chicken and some chewing gum' thing that's part of Sid play. But it was really dispiriting in late 2e when everyone else would get new shininess with every supplement and Sids.... really didn't. <b>(ADamiani)</b></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">A: The game's mechanics will grow and change as time goes on, so if we perceive a Charm that they must have, they will have it and it will thought to always be a &quot;thing&quot; in-setting. </span></span><b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 06-21-2014, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T21:02:44-07:00","id":176706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=176645#post176645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hard to say whether 1e Sidereals were successful in their purpose. They effectively existed in a vacuum, released late in the line where they didn't need to prove their effectiveness against an evolving game line. Yeah, 2e Sidereals were broken from the get-go, but I'd like to see the 1e Sidereal set put through its paces in a post-GotMH and DotFA scenario, where everyone else's Charm sets continue to expand and theirs just... stays still.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal Charm set is fixed in place to fit a specific thematic niche, and it is one that is remarkably unadaptable. For it to function, there can be <i>no</i> evolution of the game line, making everything as stagnant as itself. If the game evolves, by introducing new mechanics or that higher level of power they say they won't introduce, it all goes to hell, and either the closed Charm set has to go, or the Sidereals will forever fall behind. And if you say &quot;well, people can just ask the Maidens for new Charms, or you can introduce it retroactively,&quot; that's not actually a closed Charm set, it's just a neat but mechanically meaningless piece of fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! I see what you mean. My impression is that 3e is planning things out much more heavily from the start, and is attempting to include the entire breadth of each splat's charms in its main hardback in order to ensure that there's not a need to go back later and do the second half of everybody's charmsets. And, of course, any mid-stream changes to the line do need to consider the degree to which they'll break major blocks of material that precede them.<br /> <br /> But yeah, it is certainly possible that the line could shift in a way that leaves Sidereals in the lurch. I think that if this happens it's indicative of a broader design failing with the game line, but certainly there will be some broader design failings exposed in the first eight years of a popular RPG's life; that's inevitable. In that case I think it is fine for the writers to errata Sidereals as needed, or to retroactively add more charms to their set. The main feature of the closed charmset is that the <i>players</i> can't make new charms, because it's meant to be a carefully tuned machine, and it'd be like allowing the players to invent new moves for a WoW class, or give new specials to a fighting game character. And yet, it's fine for the <i>developers</i> to do that, so long as they do it carefully and with the original thesis of the class/character in mind. It's not closed in the sense that it's &quot;in the can&quot; and no changes can ever happen to it ever at a meta-game level, in other words, just in that it's not arbitrarily extensible, and homebrew is not endorsed for it in the same way it is for other charmsets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T21:05:25-07:00","id":176707,"title":"","content":"Without knowing what &quot;Astrology&quot; will do in 3rd edition, it's pretty hard to guess what the Sidereals will need from a charm set for 3rd edition, and thus how much they would be handicapped by a closed one. And we already know there will be Evocations alongside Sorcery and Martial Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T21:47:31-07:00","id":176720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=176111#post176111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, before we continue, can we please get the &quot;Sidereal Charms are sooooo weeeiiiiirrrddd&quot; thing to die in a fire? I made an entire thread about this before, but with only a few exceptions, 2e Sidereal Charms</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, I also thought that that you were mostly wrong in that thread, or saying things that didn't matter, but I avoided it when I realized you were arguing about the 2e Sidereal charmset. Arguing about that is a waste of time; everyone knows it sucks and fails at just about everything it sets out to do.<br /> <br /> Mostly the Sidereal charmset was designed around this idea of giving them an unusual competence grid overall, including holes in certain areas and unusual spikes of power elsewhere. The 2e charmset misunderstood all of this, and also failed to adopt them for the changes between editions, so none of these things really showed through the way they were intended to.<br /> <br /> For an example of what I'm talking about -- one thing Holden has said a lot is that he feels one of the big mistakes the 2e Sidereal charmset made was giving them Excellencies, since doing so essentially removed a ton of the holes in their charmset and made them play a lot less interestingly as a result. That one change negated a huge amount of what made Sidereals what they were, since in 1e most charmsets had a bunch of different dice-adders, but Sidereals did not. (This isn't to say that 3e Sidereals will necessarily lack them -- I've got no idea, and really given the vast differences in the system there's no reason to think that any of the old <i>mechanisms</i> for hitting that general mood will be coming back -- just an illustration of the mindset behind how they were originally designed and which is likely to inform their design in 3e. Understanding how a fan of 1e Sidereals could feel that carelessly giving them excellencies in 2e 'ruined' them tells you a lot about their intended design.)<br /> <br /> My feeling is that when you say &quot;Sidereals are not weird!, especially in the context of what you're saying in this thread, the subtext of what you're saying is &quot;I feel that designing them in this way has been a failure, and I don't want to see it in the future, especially not if it means them having a closed charmset.&quot; But that's not a particularly compelling argument when you're basing it on experiences with their 2e charmset, because their 2e charmset was crap from start to finish and has no lessons to teach anyone beyond &quot;don't totally screw up a splatbook, lol.&quot; I guarantee you that 3e Sidereals will be designed, as much as possible, without the slightest thought towards the mechanics, themes, or &quot;design principles&quot; Sidereals used in Second Edition; they're going to be based on the overall concepts of 1e Sidereals. (Obviously, very different based on both the changes between editions and attempts to fix some of 1e Sidereal's flaws -- 1e Sidereals weren't flawless -- but I'm 100% certain they're going to try and shoot for the same general goals.)<br /> <br /> So if you want to understand where they're heading, you have to look at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T22:42:27-07:00","id":176754,"title":"","content":"They had a lot of charms that were TN and die adders but they were all over the place. That's why you had hot eyes snake whispering for TN Reduction of four socialize abilities and Heart-Brightening Presentation Style for the same four abilities as a die adder. This was what made them a more versatile and yet constrained. You kind of needed sidereal astrology to take full advantage of dice pools that. Even though it was bullshit, Sidereal astrology that is, the system at least had more usefulness. You really have to look at 1e to understand why Sidereal charms worked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 06-22-2014, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T01:59:20-07:00","id":176849,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hey, Sidereal trees are just a bunch of utterly random stuff with no constraining rhyme or reason and are balanced because of careful, and disguised / hidden holes in their set, so they'd better not be able to get any new Charms or they become easy to accidentally or intentionally break (either unfun or too powerful for the setting)&quot; - I think that's wrong (although perhaps a strawman position, I have certainly seen comments in this vein).<br /> <br /> While there are carefully placed holes and spikes, Sidereals do have a constraining and structured design - short trees, themed under a Maidens and a prayer strip, generally focused on the ability and never really totally contrary to its nature, with particular Sidereal type patterns of strengths and weaknesses (see the start of the 1e Sidereals Charm chapter for starters and other patterns can be intuited from reading through the sets).<br /> <br /> But at the same time, this design does mean that opening their charmset in the sense of letting Sidereals build potentially endless ad hoc extensions to their sets probably doesn't work.<br /> <br /> If their set were to be opened, in the sense of players able to innovate new Charms, rather than the retro-active modding Fata-Ku quoted - then the design would have to be stuck with, new complete ability cascades, not new ad hoc charms. <br /> <br /> And all this would probably be so much work for designers that we would, at least, probably not see many new published Sidereal trees, other than homebrew. So the situation likely wouldn't change *that* much, except for very good homebrewers or people enthusiastic about using others homebrew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T02:40:09-07:00","id":176880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=176653#post176653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't entirely agree with this. Sure having a charm is better than having no charm at all, but there were some charms that were so prohibitively complex or punitive to use that they were hardly worthwhile. Essentially all they did was take up a spot in the tree that could have been filled by a better charm, as you would have had a hell of a time ever finding a situation to use the original. A lot of the charms with this problem were made substantially better by errata, but in a stop-gap sort of way, not really addressing the issue, just smoothing it over a bit. Sidereal charms can be strange and require outside the box thinking to use, but they need to maintain a balance of utility with the charms available to other exalts, a charm that requires you to work much harder to find ways to apply its power is quantitatively less useful than a charm that has a very direct and common function. Even if the Sidereal charm is more powerful that doesn\u2019t mean much if you may never get to use it. Much of the Sidereal charm set follows this pattern, which for many people diminishes the set as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is basicaly it. Some Sidereal Charms were <i>theorethically </i>powerful but not of any actual use in the kind of situations that a standard mixed campaign (and I've never seen a all-Sidereal campaign) presents the player characters. So those charms end up being more or less just speedbumps - Charms you have to get to progress towads your capstone but which you know are practically useless and a waste of avaluable bit of XP.<br /> <br /> My Sidereals seemed to usually end up in a situation where half their charms were used constantly and the other half were used so rarely I needed to recheck my sheet to remember what they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T05:33:36-07:00","id":176921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=176720#post176720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an example of what I'm talking about -- one thing Holden has said a lot is that he feels one of the big mistakes the 2e Sidereal charmset made was giving them Excellencies, since doing so essentially removed a ton of the holes in their charmset and made them play a lot less interestingly as a result. That one change negated a huge amount of what made Sidereals what they were, since in 1e most charmsets had a bunch of different dice-adders, but Sidereals did not. (This isn't to say that 3e Sidereals will necessarily lack them -- I've got no idea, and really given the vast differences in the system there's no reason to think that any of the old <i>mechanisms</i> for hitting that general mood will be coming back -- just an illustration of the mindset behind how they were originally designed and which is likely to inform their design in 3e. Understanding how a fan of 1e Sidereals could feel that carelessly giving them excellencies in 2e 'ruined' them tells you a lot about their intended design.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem was the decision to fold of all their TN reducers into the Fateful Excellency. Specifically the option to spend 4m 1wp to turn any dice pool into successes allowed you to opt out of the esoteric Sidereal paradigm in favour of simply winning any Bureaucracy rolls you make with a charm that makes you the very best at Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> That said (essence) was a bad idea for a dice cap given 2e's other problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T05:43:06-07:00","id":176924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=176880#post176880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is basicaly it. Some Sidereal Charms were <i>theorethically </i>powerful but not of any actual use in the kind of situations that a standard mixed campaign (and I've never seen a all-Sidereal campaign) presents the player characters. So those charms end up being more or less just speedbumps - Charms you have to get to progress towads your capstone but which you know are practically useless and a waste of avaluable bit of XP.<br /> <br /> My Sidereals seemed to usually end up in a situation where half their charms were used constantly and the other half were used so rarely I needed to recheck my sheet to remember what they were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the new Sidereals will need quite a lot of playtesting.<br /> <br /> I can understand being all like &quot;Sidereal Charms can be a bit of a puzzle to work out, that's fun&quot; but if loads of the playtesters just never find a use for them, maybe swap them out. You can't afford to have much fat in a set like the Sidereal one, with finite space and constrained paths, where the logic is that they're powerful but that's all you (at least easily) get. It's a balance between that and taking risks in putting out stuff that feels like a puzzle to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T10:18:00-07:00","id":177151,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering here that in 1e, Sidereals were encouraged to stunt using their charms in ways that technically broke the rules of the charms, and they had considerably more latitude to do this than other Exalted. 2e removed this, I think, because 2e tried to make Sidereals less weird and dialled back the &quot;rule-breaking&quot; aspect of stunts (a shame, as it was my favourite part -- but I digress). However, it's a useful illustration of the difference between Sidereal design philosophy and everyone else's, and it was meant to provide some counterbalance the scope limitations of their charms without throwing open the gates or allowing you to &quot;cheat&quot; in a reliable and repeatable fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T11:28:04-07:00","id":177206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=176921#post176921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem was the decision to fold of all their TN reducers into the Fateful Excellency. Specifically the option to spend 4m 1wp to turn any dice pool into successes allowed you to opt out of the esoteric Sidereal paradigm in favour of simply winning any Bureaucracy rolls you make with a charm that makes you the very best at Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> That said (essence) was a bad idea for a dice cap given 2e's other problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e just copied and pasted 1e. It would have required effort to give them a dice pool other than (essence).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T16:38:21-07:00","id":179328,"title":"","content":"Isn't having your charms dictated by/being the charms of someone else (The Maidens) something that everyone hated about 2e Infernals. <br /> <br /> Something I've noticed is that two abilities that keep being brought up of being iconic of Sidereals, hiding in a teacup and punching people into a duck, are not charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T17:06:25-07:00","id":179348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Indivisible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=179328#post179328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've noticed is that two abilities that keep being brought up of being iconic of Sidereals, hiding in a teacup and punching people into a duck, are not charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pattern Spider Touch doesn't <i>have</i> to be a punch, but it's absolutely capable of turning someone into a duck.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T17:09:08-07:00","id":179351,"title":"","content":"I think punching people into something else is an SMA charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T17:55:02-07:00","id":179388,"title":"","content":"Looks like I Sidereal'd you, Wizard!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T18:39:15-07:00","id":179408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=179388#post179388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like I Sidereal'd you, Wizard!</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Oe7Q8OCm5I\" target=\"_blank\">Wizard is a duck</a>, or trying to figure out how to get out of the teacup in which you've hidden him? ... Both?<br /> <br /> More on topic, I think Indivisible was going for the point that neither of them are <i>native</i> Sidereal Charms, the Charms over which the Maidens hold sway. I'm under the impression the Maidens <i>did</i> hold sway over the teacup trick, given they crafted the constellations (unless I'm off-base, there). In which case the memetic Sidereals are known for one trick the Maidens made for them and one trick they developed on their own.<br /> <br /> Unrelated to anything, I'm looking forward to EX3 Sidereal Martial Arts dipping down into &quot;Sidereal PCs have a more realistic chance of getting to use this&quot; levels. Pattern's Spider Touch within a more accessible range? Yes, please. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T20:34:13-07:00","id":179430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=179408#post179408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More on topic, I think Indivisible was going for the point that neither of them are <i>native</i> Sidereal Charms, the Charms over which the Maidens hold sway. I'm under the impression the Maidens <i>did</i> hold sway over the teacup trick, given they crafted the constellations (unless I'm off-base, there).</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed that the teacup trick was Walking Outside Fate, which isn't hiding in the teacup per say, but more hiding next to it where no one can detect you. Like, ya'know, they could be right now. Just right behind you. <br /> <br /> And the Sidereals are very disappointed in your choice of tea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unrelated to anything, I'm looking forward to EX3 Sidereal Martial Arts dipping down into &quot;Sidereal PCs have a more realistic chance of getting to use this&quot; levels. Pattern's Spider Touch within a more accessible range? Yes, please. ^_^ </div> </div> </div>Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick at chargen, go go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T20:53:50-07:00","id":179433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=179430#post179430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always assumed that the teacup trick was Walking Outside Fate, which isn't hiding in the teacup per say, but more hiding next to it where no one can detect you. Like, ya'know, they could be right now. Just right behind you.</div> </div> </div> </div>If so, I hope they're here to tidy up the place. Man, been too long since I've given my apartment a proper cleaning. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> Also, it might well be that Charm! I admit to only having read it once or twice when the Errata came out. I'd thought there was a Resplendant Destiny that could do the trick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the Sidereals are very disappointed in your choice of tea. </div> </div> </div>Of course not, I have none. I also have no sympathy for the Sidereals: they should have really seen this coming. Yeah, I went there. Come at me!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick at chargen, go go. </div> </div> </div>Touche. Amending my remark: I'm looking forward to EX3 Sidereal Martial Arts dipping down into &quot;Sidereal PCs have a more realistic chance of getting to use this&quot; levels <i>and being written with some eye for balance.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T21:03:16-07:00","id":179441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=179433#post179433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, I hope they're here to tidy up the place. Man, been too long since I've given my apartment a proper cleaning. &gt;.&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you worry! Your abode is gonna get a <i>terminal cleansing.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it might well be that Charm! I admit to only having read it once or twice when the Errata came out. I'd thought there was a Resplendant Destiny that could do the trick. </div> </div> </div>There are two ways to do it:<br /> <br /> 1) Everywhere and Nowhere Technique - Replendency of the Mask<br /> 2) God Ways - SMA charm out of Prismatic Arrangement of Creation<br /> <br /> I have no real idea which, if either of those charms inspired the teacup ninja label.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course not, I have none. I also have no sympathy for the Sidereals: they should have really seen this coming. Yeah, I went there. Come at me! </div> </div> </div>In order to do this, a Sidereal requires one of the following:<br /> <br /> Of The Shape Of The World - To determine that your teacups will not hold tea<br /> Wise Choice - To discover that in any given choice of teas which you might enjoy, you prefer a different beverage<br /> Auspicious Prospects for Serenity - See above<br /> Subordinate Inspiration Technique - To really put you in the mood for coffee<br /> Force Decision - I SAID YOU WANT COFFEE DAMMIT<br /> Pattern Spider Touch - To turn you into you, only you really only drink strawberry-flavored sodas<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Touche. Amending my remark: I'm looking forward to EX3 Sidereal Martial Arts dipping down into &quot;Sidereal PCs have a more realistic chance of getting to use this&quot; levels <i>and being written with some eye for balance.</i> </div> </div> </div>In 3e, this technique will allow you to destroy TWO Creations!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T21:56:06-07:00","id":179461,"title":"","content":"I did mean native charms. I hope 3e doesn't have Sidereals be too dependent on Martial Arts for duck punching, because that seems like the sort of thing I'd like to have as a Sidereal player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T12:09:19-07:00","id":179917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Indivisible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=179328#post179328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't having your charms dictated by/being the charms of someone else (The Maidens) something that everyone hated about 2e Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't see much dislike for Charms being defined by another being with Infernals, a lot because anyway Infernals can go down the route of custom Charms. <br /> <br /> Problems with Infernals' Charms that various (not necessarily the same) people have were <br /> <br /> - their Charms pointing at actually *being* another, more powerful alien being rather than being an Exalted. <br /> <br /> the Charms weren't defined by another being, they were about, as a distant end result (but one which people clamoured for at times), turning *into* another being. and that other being at a scale beyond what it is healthy to have most games assume they should shoot for. and beyond what the game can run very well. and in the process making lots of non-Infernals games a bit too much into about fighting these sorts of being, as well.<br /> <br /> - the Charms being kind of indifferent to what the GSP was good at and the sort of person they were.<br /> <br /> - the Charms being focused on Infernal characters (and Infernal characters enemies) grappling with the supernatural evil nature of the Charms, as opposed to grappling with other dilemmas, challenges, enemies, etc. which are a less &quot;eeeevil&quot;<br /> <br /> - the Charms being structured so that the developers would've had to write almost an Exalt splat's worth of Charms for each Infernal tree for them to be viable... and with a pattern structure that would be more difficult to balance than Ability trees are to boot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T12:49:23-07:00","id":179968,"title":"","content":"You know what I think Infernals needed? More heresy charms. Low-essence ones at that. Because think about it, what are GSPs supposed to do? Things that neither the Yozis themselves nor the Akuma can. Number one on that list? Invent new charms that mash together the themes of two or more Yozis. The Yozis are stuck in their rut. First step out of it? Heresy charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T22:55:53-07:00","id":187737,"title":"","content":"I have a question and I figured this would be the appropriate thread to ask it in.<br /> <br /> Ok I get that the Sidereals can't make custom charms in universe because The Maidens won't let them, but I wanted to know how this works. I mean I don't exactly understand how The Maidens are able to limit them from making their own. Was that ever explained?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T23:23:05-07:00","id":187751,"title":"","content":"In some ways, it's just an expression of the fundamentally different themes of each Incarna and the way those themes are expressed through the Exaltations that Incarna catalyzed. All Exalts can do similar things, their way of approaching those things is just different. <br /> <br /> Compare Solars, Lunars, and Sidereals: the former two have a way to flawlessly disguise themselves as another specific person (Solars through disguise-y Larceny Charms, Lunars through Appearance Charms, but more to the point, through Knacks); Sidereals could probably do pretty well using disguise-y Charms and Astrology, but it works in a different way. A Solar who wants to impersonate Cathak Cainan disguises themselves as Cainan, mimics his clothing, his voice, his body language...and does so so convincingly that others think the Solar is Cainan for the duration of that Charm. The Lunar eats Cainan's heart and, in many ways, <i>actually becomes him</i>; if that disguised Solar sired a child on one of Cainan's concubines, that child wouldn't look anything like Cainan, but instead like the Solar and the mother, but the Lunar effectively <i>is </i>Cainan while he wears his shape with Heart's Blood, and a child probably would actually resemble Cainan (I'm trying not to use terms like genes and DNA, because Creation's biological and physical laws don't work as a perfect of the real world, being fundamentally composed of motes and not atoms, etc). A Sidereal under a certain Resplendent Destiny, like <i>Prince of the Earth</i>, could adopt the trappings of a Dragon-Blood and perhaps even trappings that Cainan would carry, but he won't look like Cainan unless he applies other magic, even if he's able to convince people that he is actually Cathak Cainan (such people probably would not be fooled if they had ever seen or heard an accurate description of Cainan though; RDs are much better at convincingly imitating archetypes than any real person that exists anywhere else).<br /> <br /> Or with defenses: a Solar about to be hit with a sword dodges puissantly, perfectly. He is still there, in the path of the sword, but then he isn't. He's still in the area, or the scene (barring use of other Charms). Lunars, with their 2e &quot;Silver Solar&quot; flavor, pretty much work the same way: it's a puissant dodge, it's moving between the sunbeams to avoid the sword. Sidereals are just not there. They quickly write an order to the Loom and instead of being hit with a sword in Nexus, they're two streets over looking at silks, because they just altered reality. Mechanically, the effect is the same: you are perfectly not hit, but the way in which this is accomplished is very different. And that thematic difference in Charms applies to the splats as a whole. Solar and Lunar Charmsets express themselves naturally through a degree of imitation of the Incarna that catalyzed the Exaltation; by contrast, the Sidereal charm set is described as being &quot;written&quot; by the Maidens with each Ability tied to a constellation and a fundamental truth about Creation's laws, rather than expressing itself organically through the lens of the Exaltation like other Celestials' sets.<br /> <br /> The following is maybe not the best analogy but I feel like it's somewhat apt: the Sidereal Exaltation is like a closed-source OS and their native Charms are closed-source programs that run on it. Sids don't have &quot;source code&quot; access for their native powers, thus they cannot create new expressions of power from whole-cloth and tend to expand their competence through universal applications like Martial Arts and Sorcery. Every other Exalt type's Exaltation and Charm technology is more like open-source, in that an individual Exalt can develop custom expressions of their Exalted power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T10:10:11-07:00","id":188052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=187737#post187737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok I get that the Sidereals can't make custom charms in universe because The Maidens won't let them, but I wanted to know how this works. I mean I don't exactly understand how The Maidens are able to limit them from making their own. Was that ever explained?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's wrong.<br /> <br /> Sidereals can't make custom charms because that's not how a Sidereal Exaltation works. The Sidereal Exaltation grants you the ability to use certain powers, and that's it; just like a Solar Exaltation doesn't grant you the ability to shapeshift, a Lunar Exaltation doesn't surround you with raw elemental fire when your anima is flared, and a DB Exaltation doesn't grant you access to SMA, a Sidereal Exaltation doesn't grant you the ability to invent your own charms. Different Exaltations grant different types of power based on the thematics of the being that empowered them; something about the nature of the Maidens means that their Exalted get a specific suite of charms and do not get the ability (common to most other Exalted) to create new native charms from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T19:22:34-07:00","id":188369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=188052#post188052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that's wrong.<br /> <br /> Sidereals can't make custom charms because that's not how a Sidereal Exaltation works. The Sidereal Exaltation grants you the ability to use certain powers, and that's it; just like a Solar Exaltation doesn't grant you the ability to shapeshift, a Lunar Exaltation doesn't surround you with raw elemental fire when your anima is flared, and a DB Exaltation doesn't grant you access to SMA, a Sidereal Exaltation doesn't grant you the ability to invent your own charms. Different Exaltations grant different types of power based on the thematics of the being that empowered them; something about the nature of the Maidens means that their Exalted get a specific suite of charms and do not get the ability (common to most other Exalted) to create new native charms from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah was wondering since it so often crops up in threads that The Maidens don't allow Sidereals to make their own charms (hell it was this threads initial discussion topic) so I was curious how this was enforced, but if the book just says they don't have the capacity to do so then alright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T20:07:46-07:00","id":188412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Indivisible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=179328#post179328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't having your charms dictated by/being the charms of someone else (The Maidens) something that everyone hated about 2e Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>The big problem with 2e Infernal Charms was the Excellencies.<br /> The idea was that you'd have to be clever to use the Malfeas Excellency in a way Malfeas would never consider but this lead to a lot of people designing their characters personalities around the Excellencies and their limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T11:31:43-07:00","id":188828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the big problem was the &quot;Forces you to act like Yozi&quot; charms, that were mandatory to advance in the tree?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only example of this in the MoEP: Infernals sets is Witness to Darkness.<br /> Which follows the same pattern as the Excellency, in that you don't have to play its games but you suffer a (- essence) internal penalty to Charisma.<br /> Predictably most people who take this charm make characters who are Manipulation 5 Charisma 1 and argue to the bitter end that <i>everything</i> should be achievable with Manipulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T14:09:40-07:00","id":188913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=188828#post188828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Predictably most people who take this charm make characters who are Manipulation 5 Charisma 1 and argue to the bitter end that <i>everything</i> should be achievable with Manipulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness this has <i>always </i>been a problem with the WW vaguely-defined-social/mental-attribute-applicability, particularly Cha/Man (and it's so good that Exalted (at least 2e, possibly 1e) ended the bullshit moral judgment placed on Manipulation uses that dated to the earliest days of OWoD).<br /> <br /> But even other Yozi Charms that didn't give the explicit penalty of WtD at least implied that there was one way to play with that Charm, and other ways were Doing It Wrong. This is implicit in the Excellencies, being that they represent a broad swath of how a Primordial thought process operates.<br /> <br /> I see this as totally different from how the Sidereal Charmset works: Yozi Charms put you down a certain mental and spiritual path and their Excellency applicability rules push you to try and achieve all goals through methods allowing the Excellency to be applicable (and thus boost rolls in furtherance of that goal); Sidereal Charms, on the other hand, may have more specific applicability or activation conditions than other Exalts, but promote a general &quot;approach this problem sideways&quot; mentality versus changing your approach to interacting with the world only through certain action-channels to achieve your desired results. <br /> <br /> TL;DR: GSPs suffered from being constrained by the Yozi's Charm themes and trying to make all actions fit a particular set of &quot;If you do it X way, then you can apply this Excellency.&quot; Sidereals are not constrained by the Charm themes of the Maidens themselves per se, but rather by having a fixed toolkit of powers that must apply to all possible situations (until you branch out into the generalist powers of Sorcery/MA).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T18:10:00-07:00","id":189021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/174744-why-do-the-maidens-hold-sway-over-sidereal-charms?p=188828#post188828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only example of this in the MoEP: Infernals sets is Witness to Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, now. They also locked the telepathy Charm behind Hateful Wretched Noise. Telepathy: so tempting. HWN: so terrible. So very, very terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}